# Database Rules

- Use PostgreSQL through Prisma unless the existing repository establishes another approved pattern.
- Every schema change must have a migration.
- Add constraints and unique indexes for business invariants where appropriate.
- Use transactions for multi-record state changes.
- Protect inventory from overselling using safe transaction/locking strategy.
- Preserve immutable snapshots where the sprint requires historical accuracy, such as order pricing.
- Do not store raw card data.
- Do not perform destructive migration automatically.
- Migration names must explain the business change.
- Test migrations on a clean database and an existing-data scenario when relevant.
